Original commit body from 87cb0c2:

Python complex number literals (like 1+2j) are now serialized as strings
instead of causing TypeError during JSON serialization. This fixes analysis
of codebases like tensorflow that contain complex number literals.

The fix handles both:
- Pure imaginary constants (2j) -> "2j"
- Complex literals (1+2j) -> "(1+2j)"

Discovered via 12.11 bakeoff when analyzing tensorflow.
